# Front-end styles

Token values and their meanings are defined in `.codex/skills/frontend-development/SKILL.md`. This rule covers where styles go.

## Files

| File | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `src/index.css` | `:root` tokens (`--color-*`, typography sizes), base element styles |
| `src/styles/app.css` | App shell, sidebar, shared components |
| `src/styles/pages.css` | Page-specific layouts |
| `src/styles/extra.css` | Supplementary component styles |
| `src/styles/dark.css` | Every dark-mode override, under `html[data-appearance="dark"]` |

## Rules

- Use the semantic variables; do not repeat raw hex values in component selectors.

```css
/* ❌ */
.request-card { border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; color: #0f172a; }

/* ✅ */
.request-card { border: 1px solid var(--color-line); color: var(--color-ink); }
```

- When you add a light-mode color, add its dark counterpart in `dark.css` in the same change. Check contrast in both themes.
- Style Radix components by adding a `className` or targeting `.radix-themes` tokens. Do not restyle Radix internals in ways that hide focus rings or break states such as `data-state` and `data-disabled`.
- Status colors come from the existing `status` class mapping (`statusClass` in `src/app/navigation.ts`). Do not add new status colors.
- Use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for request numbers, counters, and dates.
- Put any new animation or transition behind `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`, or disable it under `reduce`.
- Reuse the existing breakpoints in `pages.css` (`1100px`, `800px`, `600px`) instead of adding new ones. By `600px`, forms are one column and request tables are cards.
- Long subjects, file names, and source excerpts use `overflow-wrap: anywhere`.
